 "_note": "R23: where Santhanam is internally inconsistent the standard Parashari table (Jagannath Hora, B.V. Raman) is used. Variants: venus.mars is [3,5,6,9,11,12]; v.56-58 (p.861), the rekha chart (p.861) and the house table (p.862) give 4 not 5, the worked example p.892 agrees with 5. moon.moon is [1,3,6,7,10,11] and moon.mars is [2,3,5,6,9,10,11]; v.46-48 (p.856, English and Sanskrit), the rekha chart (p.856, house 9 = Moon and Venus) and the house table (p.856) put the 9th-house bindu under Moon, not Mars. moon.jupiter is [1,4,7,8,10,11,12]; v.46-48 (p.856) puts Jupiter in house 2 and none in 12, the house table p.856 has 12. Values are the benefic houses (counted from the contributor, 1 = same sign). Jupiter-in-Jupiter houses 1 and 4 are omitted from the English text of verse 53 but are in the Sanskrit (jiva) and in the printed rekha count chart (p. 860: 5 in houses 1 and 4, total 56).",
